1
00:01:28,237 --> 00:01:34,076
RYOTSU THE LADIES' MAN

2
00:01:41,951 --> 00:01:43,652
It's so cold tonight.

3
00:01:43,886 --> 00:01:46,756
Nothing's gonna happen on a night like this.

4
00:01:46,956 --> 00:01:49,291
Let's just ditch patrol and head back.

5
00:01:50,192 --> 00:01:50,893
Pervert!

6
00:01:51,093 --> 00:01:53,596
Hey, this is the women's dorm of the Katsushika PD.

7
00:01:53,796 --> 00:01:55,631
Damn, he's got some nerve!

8
00:01:55,865 --> 00:01:57,600
Nakagawa, go round the front!

9
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:58,501
Got it!

10
00:02:03,973 --> 00:02:06,308
Where is he? Where is the pervert?

11
00:02:06,509 --> 00:02:08,244
You underwear thief!

12
00:02:17,653 --> 00:02:18,587
Ouch!

13
00:02:18,788 --> 00:02:21,824
Ow! Stop! I'm a police officer! Hey!

14
00:02:22,792 --> 00:02:25,895
It's me! Kankichi Ryotsu of the Kameari Park Police Station.

15
00:02:26,095 --> 00:02:28,497
Hey, it's Kankichi Ryotsu!

16
00:02:28,698 --> 00:02:31,233
-Damn you! -Ouch! I said I'm Ryotsu!

17
00:02:31,434 --> 00:02:35,237
I should've guessed Kankichi Ryotsu would steal underwear!

18
00:02:36,072 --> 00:02:38,307
Ryotsu, you're under arrest!

19
00:02:38,507 --> 00:02:40,443
Caught you red-handed, underwear thief!

20
00:02:40,976 --> 00:02:44,180
Don't be ridiculous! I'm no underwear thief!

21
00:02:44,380 --> 00:02:46,382
Then, what's in your hand?

22
00:02:46,615 --> 00:02:47,450
What?

23
00:02:48,918 --> 00:02:50,986
That's undeniable proof!

24
00:02:53,456 --> 00:02:57,526
N-No! I just happened to grab this when I fell down.

25
00:02:58,194 --> 00:03:00,629
I heard the screams, so I came in here!

26
00:03:00,830 --> 00:03:03,032
Do you think such an excuse will hold up?

27
00:03:03,265 --> 00:03:04,633
It's true!

28
00:03:04,834 --> 00:03:07,036
-Here's one more pervert! -No, I'm not!

29
00:03:09,105 --> 00:03:11,874
Nakagawa-san! No way!

30
00:03:12,108 --> 00:03:16,378
It's a misunderstanding. We heard someone scream "pervert" and came in here.

31
00:03:16,579 --> 00:03:18,514
It's no use. I told them that already.

32
00:03:18,714 --> 00:03:20,282
Oh, is that what happened?

33
00:03:20,483 --> 00:03:23,552
Oh no, we misunderstood. I'm sorry.

34
00:03:24,019 --> 00:03:27,423
Come to think of it, we were training to fight off perverts.

35
00:03:27,656 --> 00:03:29,725
We were yelling "pervert!"

36
00:03:29,959 --> 00:03:31,560
-Oh, dear. -Hey, you girls!

37
00:03:31,994 --> 00:03:34,864
You didn't believe me at all when I said the same thing.

38
00:03:35,064 --> 00:03:37,066
But you don't doubt Nakagawa for a second!

39
00:03:37,299 --> 00:03:39,869
Well, that's only natural, isn't it?

40
00:03:40,069 --> 00:03:41,504
Of course.

41
00:03:41,704 --> 00:03:44,907
On what basis do you girls judge people?

42
00:03:45,141 --> 00:03:47,076
Of course, it's their face!

43
00:03:47,610 --> 00:03:53,249
I mean, who'd trust a guy with a sweaty face and a monobrow?

44
00:03:53,449 --> 00:03:55,351
Exactly! And you've got short legs.

45
00:03:55,551 --> 00:03:57,086
-You're rough. -And pushy.

46
00:03:57,419 --> 00:03:59,421
With a weirdly long torso for a short guy.

47
00:03:59,622 --> 00:04:00,556
And your feet stink!

48
00:04:01,056 --> 00:04:03,425
-Shut your traps, you jerks! -Ryotsu, stop!

49
00:04:03,626 --> 00:04:04,627
-Let me go! -Ryotsu!

50
00:04:04,860 --> 00:04:06,395
Damn it, let me go!

51
00:04:06,595 --> 00:04:07,897
That sound can't be...

52
00:04:09,598 --> 00:04:11,534
Stop, you idiot!

53
00:04:12,868 --> 00:04:13,803
Ryo-san!

54
00:04:14,036 --> 00:04:15,704
No, it was a misunderstanding!

55
00:04:15,905 --> 00:04:17,173
Only for Nakagawa-san.

56
00:04:17,373 --> 00:04:19,108
You tried to steal our underwear.

57
00:04:19,341 --> 00:04:22,044
No, I didn't!

58
00:04:22,645 --> 00:04:24,013
A pervert.

59
00:04:24,213 --> 00:04:26,215
He's a police officer.

60
00:04:28,184 --> 00:04:33,455
I'm innocent!

61
00:04:35,391 --> 00:04:37,226
That was a tough break, Ryotsu.

62
00:04:37,426 --> 00:04:41,030
But you brought this on yourself with the way you usually behave.

63
00:04:41,597 --> 00:04:43,899
You'd better reflect on that properly.

64
00:04:44,099 --> 00:04:45,768
Reflect? Don't be ridiculous!

65
00:04:46,402 --> 00:04:49,572
Seriously, what do women these days think men are?

66
00:04:50,072 --> 00:04:52,975
Well, I can understand what you're saying.

67
00:04:53,209 --> 00:04:56,645
It's true that women these days are beyond my understanding.

68
00:04:56,845 --> 00:04:58,280
Just the other day...

69
00:04:59,081 --> 00:05:00,416
Ugh, super lame!

70
00:05:00,616 --> 00:05:01,817
Right?

71
00:05:02,284 --> 00:05:04,420
Then, with a pathetic look, he goes,

72
00:05:04,620 --> 00:05:06,689
"Please go out with me."

73
00:05:06,922 --> 00:05:08,224
Eww, what a creep.

74
00:05:08,424 --> 00:05:10,292
He's got no money or anything!

75
00:05:10,492 --> 00:05:11,227
Hey, old man!

76
00:05:11,927 --> 00:05:13,395
What are you staring at?

77
00:05:13,596 --> 00:05:14,863
N-No, I wasn't...

78
00:05:15,130 --> 00:05:16,699
Pervert.

79
00:05:16,932 --> 00:05:18,834
Well, I was completely baffled.

80
00:05:19,068 --> 00:05:20,936
They might as well be aliens.

81
00:05:21,136 --> 00:05:22,238
I've decided!

82
00:05:24,173 --> 00:05:26,108
What are you doing, Ryotsu?

83
00:05:26,308 --> 00:05:29,478
I'll never deal with women again!

84
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:34,416
No woman gets within two meters of me!

85
00:05:34,617 --> 00:05:37,853
Come on! You can't do your work like that!

86
00:05:38,187 --> 00:05:39,121
Hmph!

87
00:05:40,656 --> 00:05:43,792
Excuse me, which direction is the station?

88
00:05:43,993 --> 00:05:46,095
-Ah! No, no! -Huh?

89
00:05:46,295 --> 00:05:48,497
Shoo! Don't you dare cross that line!

90
00:05:48,998 --> 00:05:50,499
W-What did you say?

91
00:05:51,033 --> 00:05:52,835
You're a police officer, right?

92
00:05:53,035 --> 00:05:55,204
Oh, to get to the station...

93
00:05:55,638 --> 00:05:57,506
turn left at the first corner...

94
00:05:57,706 --> 00:06:00,042
Y-You...

95
00:06:00,442 --> 00:06:01,744
idiot!

96
00:06:07,850 --> 00:06:10,853
No matter what anyone says, I'll never deal with women!

97
00:06:12,588 --> 00:06:14,189
What a shame.

98
00:06:14,757 --> 00:06:17,993
We almost had Ryotsu arrested.

99
00:06:18,193 --> 00:06:19,728
That's right.

100
00:06:19,929 --> 00:06:21,697
Huh? In front of the dorm...

101
00:06:27,603 --> 00:06:30,039
Why are they putting logs in the girls' dorm yard?

102
00:06:30,372 --> 00:06:32,308
Yeah, keep coming.

103
00:06:32,508 --> 00:06:34,009
Naoko, we have a problem!

104
00:06:35,044 --> 00:06:36,612
What are these logs?

105
00:06:36,845 --> 00:06:40,182
Are you Naoko Seisho? Congratulations on your win!

106
00:06:40,683 --> 00:06:41,750
Oh, thank you.

107
00:06:41,950 --> 00:06:45,487
I see! You won that thing!

108
00:06:45,688 --> 00:06:47,723
Oh, the prize in that magazine!

109
00:06:47,923 --> 00:06:51,794
I applied for it on a whim, but never expected to actually win.

110
00:06:52,494 --> 00:06:55,064
But there's plenty of space here, so it's fine, right?

111
00:06:55,264 --> 00:06:55,965
Yeah.

112
00:06:56,198 --> 00:06:58,100
-It'll be like a dorm villa! -Nice!

113
00:06:59,101 --> 00:07:01,704
Okay, we've finished bringing in the materials.

114
00:07:02,338 --> 00:07:04,873
Here's some videos on how to assemble the log house.

115
00:07:05,207 --> 00:07:07,543
Do your best putting it together.

116
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:14,450
Huh?! We have to make it?

117
00:07:15,050 --> 00:07:17,953
What should we do? We can't put these together.

118
00:07:18,454 --> 00:07:21,190
Do you know anyone who's good at this kind of thing?

119
00:07:21,390 --> 00:07:22,891
No.

120
00:07:23,726 --> 00:07:24,960
There's one!

121
00:07:25,728 --> 00:07:26,595
But...

122
00:07:26,795 --> 00:07:28,998
He'll never do it.

123
00:07:29,665 --> 00:07:32,134
Oh, that's it! I have a good idea.

124
00:07:32,368 --> 00:07:33,635
Listen.

125
00:07:34,203 --> 00:07:36,005
Gather everyone tomorrow...

126
00:07:36,538 --> 00:07:39,074
Hey, Ryo-san! This is serious!

127
00:07:39,775 --> 00:07:42,311
Look at this month's survey in the precinct newsletter.

128
00:07:42,544 --> 00:07:43,812
Hmph, who cares?

129
00:07:44,246 --> 00:07:47,583
It's the same boring junk every month.

130
00:07:47,783 --> 00:07:50,819
Frankly, that's harassment, mocking men!

131
00:07:51,019 --> 00:07:54,089
What is it? Is Ryotsu the most disliked again?

132
00:07:54,289 --> 00:07:56,625
That'll be seven times in a row.

133
00:08:00,763 --> 00:08:01,630
What's wrong?

134
00:08:03,832 --> 00:08:05,134
What's this?

135
00:08:05,334 --> 00:08:08,170
For the man most disliked by the women of the Katsushika PD,

136
00:08:08,404 --> 00:08:10,272
Ryotsu's name isn't on the list!

137
00:08:11,273 --> 00:08:12,341
What!

138
00:08:12,875 --> 00:08:15,844
Ryo-san is ranked number one in the most liked list.

139
00:08:17,346 --> 00:08:18,847
Oh, look at this!

140
00:08:19,982 --> 00:08:22,284
The most popular man, Kankichi Ryotsu!

141
00:08:22,484 --> 00:08:25,320
The most dateable guy, Kankichi Ryotsu!

142
00:08:25,521 --> 00:08:28,023
The most marriageable man, Kankichi Ryotsu!

143
00:08:28,624 --> 00:08:31,860
Nakagawa always wins, but you beat him to the triple crown.

144
00:08:32,061 --> 00:08:34,196
Is it some kind of misprint?

145
00:08:34,430 --> 00:08:35,831
I don't think so.

146
00:08:36,031 --> 00:08:37,699
It's more than just a typo.

147
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:39,368
That means...

148
00:08:39,868 --> 00:08:42,671
You've pulled some dirty trick behind my back again!

149
00:08:42,871 --> 00:08:44,606
Why would I do such a thing?

150
00:08:44,973 --> 00:08:49,545
Chief, I don't think Ryotsu would bother to do anything that doesn't make money.

151
00:08:49,745 --> 00:08:51,547
Come to think of it, you're right.

152
00:08:52,347 --> 00:08:54,817
But jumping from the bottom to the top?

153
00:08:55,017 --> 00:08:56,084
That's strange.

154
00:08:56,318 --> 00:08:57,553
Not strange at all!

155
00:08:58,086 --> 00:09:00,556
At last, modern women have realized

156
00:09:00,756 --> 00:09:02,558
what true manliness really is.

157
00:09:03,525 --> 00:09:06,728
They have begun to choose substance over appearances.

158
00:09:09,765 --> 00:09:11,366
Ryotsu-senpai!

159
00:09:11,767 --> 00:09:13,168
For being the most popular guy...

160
00:09:13,368 --> 00:09:14,870
Congratulations!

161
00:09:15,471 --> 00:09:17,105
Congratulations on being number one!

162
00:09:17,372 --> 00:09:18,574
Oh, thanks.

163
00:09:18,774 --> 00:09:21,710
We've been wrong about you until now.

164
00:09:21,910 --> 00:09:25,214
That's right. We finally realized how attractive you are.

165
00:09:25,914 --> 00:09:27,649
H-He's very popular.

166
00:09:27,850 --> 00:09:29,118
I don't believe my eyes.

167
00:09:29,351 --> 00:09:29,952
Hmph!

168
00:09:30,385 --> 00:09:33,021
Oh, my gosh.

169
00:09:33,222 --> 00:09:35,257
Didn't you say you won't deal with women?

170
00:09:35,491 --> 00:09:36,325
What?

171
00:09:36,925 --> 00:09:38,527
What an unprincipled man!

172
00:09:39,761 --> 00:09:41,697
D-Don't cross that line!

173
00:09:41,897 --> 00:09:42,598
What?

174
00:09:43,365 --> 00:09:45,934
I've decided not to deal with women.

175
00:09:46,134 --> 00:09:47,903
Don't say such a thing.

176
00:09:48,103 --> 00:09:50,939
Shut up! Get out! Shoo!

177
00:09:52,241 --> 00:09:53,609
-Senpai, ah! -The heck with this!

178
00:09:54,142 --> 00:09:55,611
Buzz off!

179
00:09:56,545 --> 00:09:58,380
What's with that attitude?

180
00:09:58,580 --> 00:10:00,115
Come on, take it easy.

181
00:10:00,616 --> 00:10:03,085
Anyway, step one is complete.

182
00:10:03,285 --> 00:10:06,121
There's no way that idiot won't take the bait.

183
00:10:11,693 --> 00:10:14,296
"KATSUSHIKA POLICE HEADQUARTERS"

184
00:10:14,530 --> 00:10:17,166
"CONGRATULATIONS! OFFICER RYOTSU IS NUMBER ONE!"

185
00:10:17,599 --> 00:10:19,568
How about this?

186
00:10:19,768 --> 00:10:21,170
Yeah, it's pretty good.

187
00:10:22,371 --> 00:10:23,171
Here he comes!

188
00:10:23,939 --> 00:10:26,408
Hello, I'm from Rairai-ken.

189
00:10:26,842 --> 00:10:29,545
Jeez, does he think he's in disguise with that?

190
00:10:29,745 --> 00:10:30,445
Shh!

191
00:10:30,712 --> 00:10:31,980
I'm from Rairai-ken.

192
00:10:32,180 --> 00:10:34,783
I brought a bowl of ramen noodles.

193
00:10:36,652 --> 00:10:38,287
Well, thank you.

194
00:10:38,487 --> 00:10:42,124
After all, Ryotsu-senpai's charm is his manliness, right?

195
00:10:42,324 --> 00:10:43,258
I agree.

196
00:10:43,458 --> 00:10:47,663
He's got that toughness other guys are missing.

197
00:10:47,863 --> 00:10:50,332
His monobrow looks very manly too.

198
00:10:50,566 --> 00:10:54,002
A good man's really all about what's inside, not how he looks.

199
00:10:54,202 --> 00:10:59,675
But it's sad that he can't accept our passionate feelings.

200
00:10:59,875 --> 00:11:04,479
You know, we tend to rebel against the guys we like.

201
00:11:04,680 --> 00:11:05,981
It's really a bad trait.

202
00:11:06,181 --> 00:11:07,683
Oh, Ryo-sama!

203
00:11:07,883 --> 00:11:10,986
But I bet he's got lots of girls around him.

204
00:11:12,955 --> 00:11:16,225
"We tend to rebel against the guys we like."

205
00:11:16,692 --> 00:11:20,162
Well, sure, the female mind is a complicated thing.

206
00:11:21,697 --> 00:11:24,299
Hey, you two.

207
00:11:24,499 --> 00:11:26,468
Oh, Ryotsu-senpai!

208
00:11:26,668 --> 00:11:30,305
Senpai, you didn't accept our bouquet earlier.

209
00:11:31,139 --> 00:11:33,308
I was so sad.

210
00:11:33,675 --> 00:11:37,179
Well, I'm sorry about that.

211
00:11:37,379 --> 00:11:40,349
Oh, a can of coffee. It's nice on such a cold day.

212
00:11:40,549 --> 00:11:41,817
Give me a sip.

213
00:11:42,017 --> 00:11:43,452
What? Buy one your—

214
00:11:43,652 --> 00:11:44,519
Naoko!

215
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:45,520
Huh?

216
00:11:45,721 --> 00:11:47,322
Oh, please drink it.

217
00:11:47,522 --> 00:11:48,457
Okay then.

218
00:11:50,225 --> 00:11:51,360
Mmm, it's good!

219
00:11:51,560 --> 00:11:53,028
There. You drink some, too.

220
00:11:53,228 --> 00:11:54,529
Huh?!

221
00:11:54,830 --> 00:11:55,631
Hmm?

222
00:11:56,164 --> 00:11:58,066
Don't be shy. Have a drink.

223
00:11:58,267 --> 00:11:59,901
B-But...

224
00:12:03,238 --> 00:12:05,240
I'm so happy, Ryotsu-senpai.

225
00:12:11,546 --> 00:12:13,949
Woo-hoo!

226
00:12:18,020 --> 00:12:19,121
Yahoo!

227
00:12:26,028 --> 00:12:28,397
Ugh, why did I have to go through this?

228
00:12:28,597 --> 00:12:31,233
You held back well, Naoko. Well done!

229
00:12:31,933 --> 00:12:34,736
Your noble sacrifice won't be in vain!

230
00:12:35,404 --> 00:12:37,039
Time to wrap this up!

231
00:12:41,276 --> 00:12:43,879
"KAMEARI PARK POLICE STATION"

232
00:12:52,688 --> 00:12:54,323
Hey, Ryotsu, my man!

233
00:12:57,726 --> 00:12:59,695
Are you free tonight?

234
00:13:00,328 --> 00:13:03,165
How about going out for a drink? It's been a while.

235
00:13:03,632 --> 00:13:04,433
Huh?

236
00:13:08,337 --> 00:13:11,807
Oh, it's you, Honda-kun. How are you doing?

237
00:13:12,007 --> 00:13:14,543
W-What's going on with that look?

238
00:13:14,743 --> 00:13:18,013
I have an appointment tonight.

239
00:13:18,246 --> 00:13:21,350
I'm sorry to say, but I have no time to hang out with you.

240
00:13:21,583 --> 00:13:23,285
An appointment?

241
00:13:23,485 --> 00:13:27,155
Ryo-san is invited to the women's dorm tonight.

242
00:13:27,355 --> 00:13:28,990
The women's dorm?

243
00:13:30,559 --> 00:13:33,929
You might be jealous, but I can't take you with me.

244
00:13:34,129 --> 00:13:38,600
I'm the only one who has been invited, because I'm the most popular guy.

245
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:44,139
Women these days really know what's good about men.

246
00:13:44,606 --> 00:13:47,843
That's completely different from what you usually say.

247
00:13:48,043 --> 00:13:50,312
Everyone in the women's dorm!

248
00:13:50,645 --> 00:13:54,750
Good evening!

249
00:13:56,985 --> 00:13:59,354
Wow! How wonderful!

250
00:14:04,126 --> 00:14:05,794
"WELCOME, RYOTSU-SENPAI!"

251
00:14:06,361 --> 00:14:10,132
As you know, men are not allowed in here.

252
00:14:10,332 --> 00:14:12,834
You're a special exception, Ryotsu-senpai.

253
00:14:14,936 --> 00:14:17,339
Well, I'm really moved.

254
00:14:18,707 --> 00:14:20,075
Never thought I'd hear that!

255
00:14:22,511 --> 00:14:23,478
Naoko.

256
00:14:23,979 --> 00:14:24,946
Right.

257
00:14:26,014 --> 00:14:29,818
Ryotsu-senpai, the moon is so beautiful. Let's go take a look.

258
00:14:30,018 --> 00:14:32,654
Hmm? It was cloudy when I came here earlier.

259
00:14:32,854 --> 00:14:34,022
It's okay.

260
00:14:36,525 --> 00:14:37,526
All right, now!

261
00:14:38,059 --> 00:14:39,027
Roger!

262
00:14:44,166 --> 00:14:45,066
Wow!

263
00:14:46,268 --> 00:14:48,970
This is the famous "Bichunen" sake.

264
00:14:49,171 --> 00:14:50,105
Jeez!

265
00:14:54,342 --> 00:14:55,977
Oh, what on earth is that?

266
00:14:56,178 --> 00:14:58,513
That? It's a log house kit.

267
00:14:58,980 --> 00:15:02,717
All the logs are there, so we just need to follow the plans.

268
00:15:02,918 --> 00:15:04,386
Gas and water are simple too.

269
00:15:04,586 --> 00:15:08,457
If we build it in the dorm yard, it'll be a place for everyone to relax...

270
00:15:08,690 --> 00:15:11,359
But we don't have a log builder.

271
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:14,095
We can't assemble something like that.

272
00:15:14,362 --> 00:15:17,833
Oh, I wonder if there's a strong and tough guy somewhere.

273
00:15:18,033 --> 00:15:19,234
There isn't.

274
00:15:19,434 --> 00:15:21,837
All men these days are weak.

275
00:15:22,270 --> 00:15:25,874
I think guys who work hard and sweat are attractive.

276
00:15:26,074 --> 00:15:30,212
Yeah. The latest trend is men who smell like sweat.

277
00:15:30,412 --> 00:15:32,147
I don't know about any trend,

278
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:35,050
but aren't you guys forgetting someone?

279
00:15:35,250 --> 00:15:36,585
Oh, who?

280
00:15:36,785 --> 00:15:39,855
A strong, tough, dependable guy.

281
00:15:41,857 --> 00:15:43,325
What? Who?

282
00:15:45,594 --> 00:15:48,730
Oh, are you perhaps talking about yourself?

283
00:15:48,930 --> 00:15:51,900
No way, we can't ask you to do something like that!

284
00:15:52,100 --> 00:15:52,934
Why not?

285
00:15:53,235 --> 00:15:57,806
Because you're all dressed up in a sharp suit like that.

286
00:15:58,039 --> 00:15:58,640
Right.

287
00:16:00,308 --> 00:16:02,177
This is just a disguise.

288
00:16:05,881 --> 00:16:08,583
This is the real me!

289
00:16:09,317 --> 00:16:10,952
Wow! So cool!

290
00:16:11,353 --> 00:16:13,822
And this is my army!

291
00:16:14,055 --> 00:16:15,824
I'm supposed to be off duty.

292
00:16:16,057 --> 00:16:17,526
He's so pushy.

293
00:16:17,759 --> 00:16:19,427
Shut up! Stop whining!

294
00:16:19,895 --> 00:16:22,931
First, the foundation work! Got it, guys?

295
00:16:23,131 --> 00:16:24,165
Yeah.

296
00:16:25,901 --> 00:16:27,335
Get to work!

297
00:16:27,536 --> 00:16:28,603
Yeah.

298
00:16:28,803 --> 00:16:30,839
Hey! Move faster!

299
00:16:31,072 --> 00:16:33,208
Honda! What's with that awkward posture?

300
00:16:33,542 --> 00:16:35,944
-Men are so simple. -Terai!

301
00:16:45,453 --> 00:16:47,556
Hey, carry faster!

302
00:16:48,323 --> 00:16:51,860
Listen, let's coax those two into working harder as well.

303
00:16:52,627 --> 00:16:55,030
Gentlemen, it's lunch time!

304
00:16:55,497 --> 00:16:57,666
We made them ourselves.

305
00:16:57,866 --> 00:16:59,401
The cookies are homemade too.

306
00:17:00,135 --> 00:17:01,102
Wow, that's amazing.

307
00:17:01,303 --> 00:17:02,137
They look delicious!

308
00:17:02,537 --> 00:17:04,506
Thank you, Terai-san and Honda-san.

309
00:17:04,706 --> 00:17:06,174
Good luck!

310
00:17:06,374 --> 00:17:08,143
-We're counting on you. -Well...

311
00:17:08,343 --> 00:17:11,146
You're much stronger than you look, Honda-san.

312
00:17:11,346 --> 00:17:12,414
Do you think so?

313
00:17:12,647 --> 00:17:15,150
Terai-san, you have such muscly arms too!

314
00:17:15,350 --> 00:17:17,585
Oh no, it's mostly flab.

315
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:20,388
You guys, go home now!

316
00:17:20,889 --> 00:17:21,890
Darn it!

317
00:17:22,357 --> 00:17:24,726
Oh, but they've come all the way here.

318
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:26,828
I think you should all work together.

319
00:17:27,028 --> 00:17:29,164
I can handle this all by myself!

320
00:17:29,364 --> 00:17:31,700
-Go on, beat it! -We haven't finished eating.

321
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:33,668
This is terrible!

322
00:17:38,907 --> 00:17:41,242
That was a bit of a tactical mistake.

323
00:17:47,749 --> 00:17:50,752
I guess it was too difficult to do it alone after all.

324
00:17:50,986 --> 00:17:52,921
And I can't ask those guys again.

325
00:17:53,421 --> 00:17:55,757
The pace is still too slow.

326
00:17:56,391 --> 00:18:00,629
We'll thoroughly praise, flatter, and get him to work!

327
00:18:00,862 --> 00:18:01,596
Okay!

328
00:18:02,831 --> 00:18:04,232
Ryotsu-san, keep it up!

329
00:18:04,432 --> 00:18:05,367
You can do it!

330
00:18:05,567 --> 00:18:06,368
Oh?

331
00:18:06,568 --> 00:18:08,370
You look great working there!

332
00:18:08,570 --> 00:18:09,404
So cool!

333
00:18:09,604 --> 00:18:10,438
R-Really?

334
00:18:12,474 --> 00:18:14,075
Wow, I'm surprised!

335
00:18:14,275 --> 00:18:15,610
You're so strong!

336
00:18:15,844 --> 00:18:17,312
This is nothing at all!

337
00:18:19,080 --> 00:18:19,714
So nice!

338
00:18:19,914 --> 00:18:21,249
So manly!

339
00:18:21,449 --> 00:18:23,084
Hmm, do you think so?

340
00:18:24,219 --> 00:18:25,954
Look at that enthusiasm.

341
00:18:26,554 --> 00:18:28,623
Fools are easy to handle, aren't they?

342
00:18:28,857 --> 00:18:31,760
Let's keep him motivated like this around the clock in shifts.

343
00:18:31,960 --> 00:18:34,129
Hey, Ryotsu-san!

344
00:18:38,867 --> 00:18:40,435
You're so manly!

345
00:18:40,735 --> 00:18:41,770
This is nothing...

346
00:18:41,970 --> 00:18:44,205
Ryotsu-san!

347
00:18:46,574 --> 00:18:49,678
Ryotsu-senpai, so nice!

348
00:18:51,646 --> 00:18:55,150
Ryotsu-san, keep going!

349
00:18:57,152 --> 00:18:59,220
Looks like just cheering isn't enough anymore.

350
00:18:59,421 --> 00:19:03,525
Heh! I think it's time to give him a little boost.

351
00:19:05,593 --> 00:19:07,095
Ryotsu-san, are you all right?

352
00:19:07,295 --> 00:19:08,530
I'm a little bit tired.

353
00:19:10,365 --> 00:19:11,833
We'll give you a massage.

354
00:19:12,067 --> 00:19:13,334
Good luck.

355
00:19:13,535 --> 00:19:16,104
Build our log house quickly.

356
00:19:16,304 --> 00:19:18,106
Of course.

357
00:19:19,607 --> 00:19:20,508
I'm revived!

358
00:19:20,709 --> 00:19:22,110
We did it!

359
00:19:22,310 --> 00:19:24,112
Here I go!

360
00:19:24,546 --> 00:19:26,381
You can do it!

361
00:19:38,159 --> 00:19:39,294
Here's your lunch.

362
00:19:39,661 --> 00:19:40,395
See you later.

363
00:19:40,628 --> 00:19:41,963
You're leaving already?

364
00:19:42,163 --> 00:19:43,298
I-I have to work.

365
00:19:44,165 --> 00:19:46,267
Another convenience store lunch.

366
00:19:46,468 --> 00:19:49,304
It used to be a lunch homemade with love.

367
00:19:50,038 --> 00:19:54,476
As more of the log house gets completed, the quality of my lunch keeps dropping.

368
00:19:56,945 --> 00:19:58,880
Huh? This again.

369
00:19:59,547 --> 00:20:02,383
It's been a roll and butter for days now.

370
00:20:03,151 --> 00:20:07,889
No one comes to cheer me on lately, and I feel like I'm being forced to work.

371
00:20:08,723 --> 00:20:11,025
If you keep doing this, you'll break your body.

372
00:20:11,659 --> 00:20:16,998
I feel like you're being manipulated by those girls.

373
00:20:17,298 --> 00:20:18,733
Nakagawa-kun.

374
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:22,237
I know you're upset because you lost top spot to me.

375
00:20:22,437 --> 00:20:26,307
You may be jealous, but don't make strange assumptions.

376
00:20:26,508 --> 00:20:29,077
I'm not really jealous though.

377
00:20:36,251 --> 00:20:39,053
Damn, I'm really tired.

378
00:20:41,055 --> 00:20:43,691
Senpai! Ryotsu-senpai!

379
00:20:43,892 --> 00:20:45,360
Ryotsu-senpai!

380
00:20:45,560 --> 00:20:46,761
Senpai!

381
00:20:47,328 --> 00:20:49,797
Jeez! That darn Ryotsu isn't here yet.

382
00:20:50,031 --> 00:20:51,232
He bailed on us.

383
00:20:51,432 --> 00:20:53,801
It's almost finished, and he's no help at all.

384
00:20:54,035 --> 00:20:55,904
I wonder when it'll be ready.

385
00:20:56,104 --> 00:20:57,772
I'm tired of flattering him.

386
00:20:58,006 --> 00:20:58,773
What?

387
00:20:59,340 --> 00:21:02,944
Aw, we went through so much effort to get him first place in the survey.

388
00:21:03,244 --> 00:21:04,546
Just be patient a little longer.

389
00:21:06,414 --> 00:21:07,382
I'm sorry.

390
00:21:07,582 --> 00:21:09,350
We didn't mean any harm.

391
00:21:11,119 --> 00:21:14,222
Whew. What's wrong? Did you say something?

392
00:21:16,057 --> 00:21:18,660
-Nothing, nothing. -Never mind.

393
00:21:19,194 --> 00:21:21,763
Okay, almost there. Let's go for it.

394
00:21:21,963 --> 00:21:24,065
What a relief. I guess he didn't hear us.

395
00:21:24,265 --> 00:21:25,934
I'm glad he's such an idiot.

396
00:21:26,134 --> 00:21:27,368
Shh! He'll hear you.

397
00:21:35,743 --> 00:21:37,679
I'll show you.

398
00:21:43,852 --> 00:21:46,621
Wow, this is amazing!

399
00:21:47,088 --> 00:21:48,756
It's finally finished.

400
00:21:48,957 --> 00:21:50,391
Our villa.

401
00:21:51,693 --> 00:21:53,161
It's wonderful!

402
00:21:53,394 --> 00:21:54,863
The smell of wood!

403
00:21:55,496 --> 00:21:57,398
Oh, skylights!

404
00:21:57,966 --> 00:21:58,967
Wow!

405
00:21:59,167 --> 00:22:01,102
Oh, the bath is bigger than in the plans!

406
00:22:01,703 --> 00:22:03,671
Hey, let's stay here tonight.

407
00:22:03,872 --> 00:22:05,340
I agree!

408
00:22:07,642 --> 00:22:10,178
I'll show you exactly what happens

409
00:22:10,411 --> 00:22:12,614
when you make me mad.

410
00:22:15,149 --> 00:22:18,186
Ah, it feels good.

411
00:22:18,553 --> 00:22:21,356
Oh, the smell of this wood is so nice!

412
00:22:21,556 --> 00:22:24,359
I feel like I'm at a hot spring deep in the mountains.

413
00:22:24,692 --> 00:22:27,662
You know, I didn't expect him to build such a nice log house.

414
00:22:27,862 --> 00:22:29,364
Not bad at all.

415
00:22:29,964 --> 00:22:33,534
Yeah, he really worked hard.

416
00:22:33,902 --> 00:22:36,037
I've started to think better of him.

417
00:22:36,638 --> 00:22:37,906
Komachi-chan.

418
00:22:38,139 --> 00:22:38,873
W-What?

419
00:22:39,107 --> 00:22:41,809
You've fallen for Kankichi Ryotsu, haven't you?

420
00:22:42,310 --> 00:22:43,745
N-No way!

421
00:22:43,978 --> 00:22:45,113
Oh, you're blushing!

422
00:22:45,313 --> 00:22:47,015
I'm not!

423
00:22:48,449 --> 00:22:51,452
Everyone, please be quiet.

424
00:22:51,653 --> 00:22:53,288
Special seats are 5,000 yen.

425
00:22:53,488 --> 00:22:57,125
It's an extra 1,000 yen if you've brought a camera or video camera.

426
00:22:57,325 --> 00:22:58,926
Here we go!

427
00:23:01,129 --> 00:23:02,897
Divine punishment, you foolish women!

428
00:23:06,901 --> 00:23:08,236
Huh? What?

429
00:23:25,687 --> 00:23:29,023
How's that? This is what a real man can build!

430
00:23:29,223 --> 00:23:31,926
What have you done, you beast!

431
00:23:32,727 --> 00:23:35,530
This is awful! The mini patrol cars are a total mess!

432
00:23:35,730 --> 00:23:36,764
"IDIOTS"

433
00:23:37,198 --> 00:23:38,533
The tires are gone too!

434
00:23:39,901 --> 00:23:41,536
We won't forgive you!

435
00:23:42,971 --> 00:23:44,973
My revenge has just begun!

436
00:23:45,206 --> 00:23:47,975
I'll never forgive you for bullying weak women!

437
00:23:48,209 --> 00:23:50,545
What's weak about you guys?

438
00:23:50,745 --> 00:23:52,113
What did you say?

439
00:23:52,347 --> 00:23:55,516
Looks like he's about to reclaim the title of most disliked man.

440
00:23:55,717 --> 00:23:57,185
TODAY'S DAMAGE REPORT

441
00:23:57,385 --> 00:24:02,523
5 MINI PATROL CARS

442
00:24:03,191 --> 00:24:09,030
NEW YEAR'S KARUTA BATTLE!
